Relevant columns and their potential usage  

`fec.individuals_ingest_2020`  
• `state`: identify NY contributors (WHERE state = 'NY')  
• `zip_code`: 5‑digit ZIP for geographic mapping (JOIN on cross‑walk)  
• `transaction_amt`: dollar amount of each contribution (AVG / SUM for donation metrics)  

`hud_zipcode_crosswalk.zipcode_to_census_tracts`  
• `zip_code`: 5‑digit USPS ZIP (JOIN key to donors)  
• `census_tract_geoid`: 11‑digit tract GEOID (maps to ACS `geo_id`)  
• `total_ratio` (or `residential_ratio`): optional weight when a ZIP maps to several tracts  

`census_bureau_acs.censustract_2018_5yr`  
• `geo_id`: tract GEOID (JOIN key to cross‑walk)  
• `median_income`: ACS 5‑year 2018 median household income (select for output)  

Key filter conditions  
• Donors in New York: `state = 'NY'`  
• 5‑digit donor ZIP present: `zip_code IS NOT NULL`  
• Kings County (Brooklyn) tracts only: `geo_id LIKE '36047%'` (state 36, county 047)  

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten progressively richer exploratory queries
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at a handful of NY contributions.
SELECT zip_code, transaction_amt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020`
WHERE state = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) List the distinct two–letter state codes in the FEC file.
SELECT DISTINCT state
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Quick stats on contribution amounts for NY donors.
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS cnt,
  AVG(transaction_amt) AS avg_amt,
  MAX(transaction_amt) AS max_amt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020`
WHERE state = 'NY'
  AND transaction_amt IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Inspect how ZIP codes are formatted; pull the first 5 digits.
SELECT
  zip_code,
  SUBSTR(zip_code, 1, 5) AS zip5,
  COUNT(*) AS rows_in_zip
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020`
WHERE state = 'NY'
GROUP BY zip_code, zip5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) See how many NY donor ZIPs successfully match the HUD cross‑walk.
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT SUBSTR(i.zip_code,1,5)) AS ny_donor_zips,
  COUNT(DISTINCT z.zip_code)             AS matched_zips
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020` AS i
LEFT JOIN `bigquery-public-data.hud_zipcode_crosswalk.zipcode_to_census_tracts` AS z
  ON z.zip_code = SUBSTR(i.zip_code,1,5)
WHERE i.state = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Retrieve a sample of tract GEOIDs that NY contributors map into.
SELECT DISTINCT
  z.census_tract_geoid
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020` AS i
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.hud_zipcode_crosswalk.zipcode_to_census_tracts` AS z
  ON z.zip_code = SUBSTR(i.zip_code,1,5)
WHERE i.state = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Show Brooklyn (Kings Co.) tract IDs together with median income.
SELECT geo_id, median_income
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.censustract_2018_5yr`
WHERE geo_id LIKE '36047%'          -- 36=NY, 047=Kings Co.
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Average donation amount per census tract across all NY donors.
SELECT
  z.census_tract_geoid AS tract_geoid,
  AVG(i.transaction_amt) AS avg_donation
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020` AS i
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.hud_zipcode_crosswalk.zipcode_to_census_tracts` AS z
  ON z.zip_code = SUBSTR(i.zip_code,1,5)
WHERE i.state = 'NY'
  AND i.transaction_amt IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY tract_geoid
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Same as #8 but restricted to Kings County tracts only.
SELECT
  z.census_tract_geoid AS tract_geoid,
  AVG(i.transaction_amt) AS avg_donation
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020` AS i
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.hud_zipcode_crosswalk.zipcode_to_census_tracts` AS z
  ON z.zip_code = SUBSTR(i.zip_code,1,5)
WHERE i.state = 'NY'
  AND i.transaction_amt IS NOT NULL
  AND z.census_tract_geoid LIKE '36047%'
GROUP BY tract_geoid
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) FINAL — average donation and median income for every Kings‑County tract.
SELECT
  acs.geo_id                          AS census_tract_geoid,
  AVG(i.transaction_amt)              AS avg_donation_amt,
  acs.median_income
FROM `bigquery-public-data.fec.individuals_ingest_2020` AS i
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.hud_zipcode_crosswalk.zipcode_to_census_tracts` AS z
  ON z.zip_code = SUBSTR(i.zip_code,1,5)
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.censustract_2018_5yr` AS acs
  ON acs.geo_id = z.census_tract_geoid
WHERE i.state = 'NY'
  AND z.census_tract_geoid LIKE '36047%'   -- Kings County
  AND i.transaction_amt IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY census_tract_geoid, acs.median_income
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is capped with `LIMIT 20` so you can quickly inspect the output before moving on to full‑scale analysis.
